.TH sextant 1 "sextant 1.1.5"
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
sextant \- terminal SSH dashboard & server manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sextant
.RI [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sextant
is the terminal client of Sextant. It keeps every server you manage in one
dashboard: live CPU, RAM and disk, a full PTY terminal per host, an SFTP
browser, snippets that run on many hosts at once, local and dynamic port
forwarding, and a one-click SSH key setup.
.PP
The desktop client is
.BR sextant-gui (1).
Both frontends share the same engine and the same configuration files, so a
host added in one appears in the other.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B help
Print a short usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B sync
Push or pull the encrypted configuration bundle
.RB ( push | pull " with " --local " or " --webdav ).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B EDITOR
The editor opened when a remote file is edited from the SFTP browser
(defaults to
.BR vi (1)).
.TP
.B SEXTANT_PORTABLE
When set to
.BR 1 ,
configuration is stored next to the executable instead of in the user
configuration directory. A file named
.B sextant.portable
(or
.BR portable )
next to the executable has the same effect.
.SH FILES
Configuration is stored as JSON in the Sextant configuration directory:
.BR ~/.config/sextant
on Linux,
.BR "~/Library/Application Support/sextant"
on macOS and
.BR "%APPDATA%\\sextant"
on Windows.
.TP
.B settings.json
Interface, terminal and notification settings.
.TP
.B hosts.json
Saved hosts and groups. Secret values are referenced by ID, never stored here.
.TP
.B snippets.json
Saved commands.
.TP
.B secrets.json, secrets.key
Encrypted credentials. The key file is mode 0600 by default; a master
password (Argon2id) can be enabled instead.
.TP
.B state.json
Window and session state.
.TP
.B known_hosts
Host keys learned on first use, in OpenSSH format.
.PP
The OpenSSH client configuration
.RB ( ~/.ssh/config )
is read, never written. Literal
.B Host
blocks override wildcard defaults.
